-- title:
--   A lattice is determined by g₂ and g₃
-- statement:
--   The statement concerns two period pairs $L$ and $L'$, i.e. two terms of the type `PeriodPair` of pairs of complex numbers that are linearly independent over $\mathbb{R}$; to such a pair are attached the lattice $L.\mathrm{lattice} = \mathbb{Z}\omega_1 + \mathbb{Z}\omega_2$, the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{C}$ generated by the two periods, and the Weierstrass invariants $L.g_2 = 60\sum_{0 \neq \lambda \in \Lambda} \lambda^{-4}$ and $L.g_3 = 140\sum_{0 \neq \lambda \in \Lambda} \lambda^{-6}$, where $\Lambda$ is that lattice. Under the two hypotheses that $L.g_2 = L'.g_2$ and $L.g_3 = L'.g_3$, the conclusion is that $L.\mathrm{lattice} = L'.\mathrm{lattice}$, an equality of subgroups of $\mathbb{C}$. Note that only the lattices, and not the period pairs themselves, are asserted to agree: two different bases of one and the same lattice have the same invariants, and the statement says precisely that no further collapsing occurs.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the uniformisation theorem for complex elliptic curves: the assignment sending a lattice $\Lambda \subset \mathbb{C}$ to the pair $(g_2(\Lambda), g_3(\Lambda))$ is injective. It is used for the rigidity statements [`ModularCurve.exists_smul_eq_of_E4_cube_div_discriminant_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_smul_eq_of_E4_cube_div_discriminant_eq), [`ModularForm.exists_gamma0_apply_mul_apply_ne_of_forall_smul_ne`](thm.html#ModularForm.exists_gamma0_apply_mul_apply_ne_of_forall_smul_ne) and [`PeriodPair.scale_lattice_eq_of_pow_four_eq_one_or_g2_eq_zero`](thm.html#PeriodPair.scale_lattice_eq_of_pow_four_eq_one_or_g2_eq_zero), which translate equalities of modular invariants into relations between lattices and hence into $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$-equivalences of points of the upper half-plane.
